    {
      "id": "claim_d702919ba366415b81482e6432491b36",
      "statement": "Password hashing is two-stage: the client derives an argon2id hash salted with `SERVICE_SALT` plus the username (fixed 16-byte salt constant, parameters documented on `PublicApi.login()`), and the server applies one more SHA-256 round, storing only that hash-of-hash.",
      "evidence": [
